   "date": "2019-08-31T14:57:11Z",
   "subject": "Questions about CODEX2",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif;line-height:1.6\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"font-size:14px;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:22.4px\"><br></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font size=\"2\">Dear professor Jiang:</font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font size=\"2\"> </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font style=\"display:inline;font-size:13px;font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);font-weight:400;font-style:normal\">Excuse me ! My name is Yi Zhang. </font><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> I want to analyze CNVs from whole exome sequencing data. And </span></font><span style=\"font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I have some questions about the software “CODEX2&quot;. </span><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">In the part of  </span></font><span style=\"font-size:small;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\">running CODEX2 without specifying negative control  samples/regions, I have to set chr.index. I want to analyze all chromosomes. So I want to know if I need to set chr.index. For example, </span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-break:break-all;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-size:inherit;padding:0px;color:inherit;background-color:transparent;border-radius:0px\">#chr &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">20</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(96,160,176);font-style:italic\"># This can be run for one chromosome or multiple chromosomes</span>\n#chr.index &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">which</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">seqnames</span>(ref_qc)==chr)\nnormObj.null &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">normalize_null</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">Y_qc =</span> Y_qc,\n                               <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">gc_qc =</span> gc_qc,\n                               <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">K =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">1</span>:<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">5</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">N =</span> N)</code></pre></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">So  in segmentation part,  whether I need to set chr? just like </div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-break:break-all;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-size:inherit;padding:0px;color:inherit;background-color:transparent;border-radius:0px\">finalcall.CBS &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">segmentCBS</span>(Y_qc,  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(96,160,176);font-style:italic\"># recommended</span>\n                            Yhat.ns, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">optK =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">which.max</span>(BIC.ns),\n                            <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">K =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">1</span>:<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">5</span>,\n                            <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">sampname_qc =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">colnames</span>(Y_qc),\n                            <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">ref_qc =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">ranges</span>(ref_qc),\n                            <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">lmax =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">400</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">mode =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\">&quot;integer&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">And finally, I want to filter CNV  from the result of finalcall.CBS( is it suitable?).  How should I choose specific standards? <font style=\"display:inline;font-size:13px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);font-weight:400;font-style:normal\">（like lratio &gt; ? and so on</font>）</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><font style=\"display:inline;font-size:13px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);font-weight:400;font-style:normal\">Thank you, and I look forward to hearing from you.</font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Best regards,</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Yi Zhang</div></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:#909090;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12px\">------------------</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;font-family:Verdana;color:#000\"><div>zhangyi</div><div><br></div></div></div><div> </div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "eQwlA6r2BQAJ",
   "from": "Yuchao Jiang",
   "author": "94ec915e8ce36448",
   "date": "2019-09-01T14:59:05Z",
   "subject": "Re: [codex_wes_cnv] Questions about CODEX2",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi<div><br></div><div>Thanks for your interest in CODEX2. </div><div><br></div><div>No, if you want to run normalization by CODEX2 across the entire genome, you don’t need the chr.index argument. However, for segmentation, since it applies to each chromosome separately, you will need to provide with the chr.index argument.</div><div><br></div><div>For targeted sequencing though, since the targets are very sparse, segmentation is performed within each gene. See here for more details <a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/CODEX2#codex2-for-targeted-sequencing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/CODEX2%23codex2-for-targeted-sequencing&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243780302000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3dn1mLmzdoLzv-tXlbkX9k\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/CODEX2#codex2-for-targeted-sequencing</a></div><div><br></div><div>Hope that this helps with clarification. Please let us know if you have further questions.</div><div><br></div><div>Yuchao</div><div><br></div><div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Aug 31, 2019, at 10:57 AM, zhangyi &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">10452...@qq.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif;line-height:1.6\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"font-size:14px;margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;line-height:22.4px\"><br></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font size=\"2\">Dear professor Jiang:</font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font size=\"2\"> </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font style=\"display:inline;font-size:13px;font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);font-weight:400;font-style:normal\">Excuse me ! My name is Yi Zhang. </font><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif\"> I want to analyze CNVs from whole exome sequencing data. And </span></font><span style=\"font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif;font-size:small\">I have some questions about the software “CODEX2&quot;. </span><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:微软雅黑,Verdana,&quot;Microsoft Yahei&quot;,SimSun,sans-serif\">In the part of  </span></font><span style=\"font-size:small;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\">running CODEX2 without specifying negative control  samples/regions, I have to set chr.index. I want to analyze all chromosomes. So I want to know if I need to set chr.index. For example, </span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-break:break-all;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-size:inherit;padding:0px;color:inherit;background-color:transparent;border-radius:0px\">#chr &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">20</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(96,160,176);font-style:italic\"># This can be run for one chromosome or multiple chromosomes</span>\r\n#chr.index &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">which</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">seqnames</span>(ref_qc)==chr)\r\nnormObj.null &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">normalize_null</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">Y_qc =</span> Y_qc,\r\n                               <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">gc_qc =</span> gc_qc,\r\n                               <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">K =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">1</span>:<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">5</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">N =</span> N)</code></pre></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">So  in segmentation part,  whether I need to set chr? just like </div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-break:break-all;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-size:inherit;padding:0px;color:inherit;background-color:transparent;border-radius:0px\">finalcall.CBS &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">segmentCBS</span>(Y_qc,  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(96,160,176);font-style:italic\"># recommended</span>\r\n                            Yhat.ns, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">optK =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">which.max</span>(BIC.ns),\r\n                            <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">K =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">1</span>:<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">5</span>,\r\n                            <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">sampname_qc =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">colnames</span>(Y_qc),\r\n                            <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">ref_qc =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold\">ranges</span>(ref_qc),\r\n                            <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">lmax =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112)\">400</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(144,32,0)\">mode =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160)\">&quot;integer&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">And finally, I want to filter CNV  from the result of finalcall.CBS( is it suitable?).  How should I choose specific standards? <font style=\"display:inline;font-size:13px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);font-weight:400;font-style:normal\">（like lratio &gt; ? and so on</font>）</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><font style=\"display:inline;font-size:13px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);font-weight:400;font-style:normal\">Thank you, and I look forward to hearing from you.</font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Best regards,</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Yi Zhang</div></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:#909090;font-family:Arial Narrow;font-size:12px\">------------------</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;font-family:Verdana\"><div>zhangyi</div><div><br></div></div></div><div> </div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;CODEX/CODEX2 for CNV detection&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">codex2+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/codex2/tencent_03CC9D459F4E82FF7CF1873784BFD9181006%40qq.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/codex2/tencent_03CC9D459F4E82FF7CF1873784BFD9181006%2540qq.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243780302000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1rK5ccfXbZ46ZxFydPiSa-\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/codex2/tencent_03CC9D459F4E82FF7CF1873784BFD9181006%40qq.com</a>.<br>\r\n</div></blockquote></div><br></div></div>"
